course: dictionary
lesson: 6723
title: Offspring: the young of plants and animals
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Offspring means the young that a living thing makes. An animal's offspring are its babies, and a plant's offspring are its seeds. Read the example: «A studbook records every animal of one kind in zoos: its parents, birth, moves and offspring.» The words around offspring are parents and birth, so offspring must be the young animals that come from those parents.
explain: Sometimes people use offspring in a joking or formal way to mean their children. A parent might say «my offspring» with a smile, and everyone knows they mean their kids. In science lessons, offspring is used when we talk about how features pass from parents to young, which is called inheritance.
explain: Offspring has the same form for one and for many. You can say one offspring or three offspring; the word does not change. Look for the clues around it, such as parents, babies or seeds, and check that your meaning still makes sense in the sentence.
fact: Offspring means the young of an animal or plant.
fact: The offspring of a plant can be its seeds.
fact: In «parents and offspring», offspring means the children or young that come from the parents.
fact: Offspring is the same word for one and for many.
fact: Scientists study how parents pass features to their offspring.
exercise: In «A studbook records every animal of one kind in zoos: its parents, birth, moves and offspring», what does offspring mean? | The keepers who look after the animals | The oldest animals in the zoo | The moves between zoos | *The young that come from the animals
exercise: A tree drops seeds that grow into new trees. What word fits? The seeds are the tree's | *offspring | shadows | parents
exercise: Dad jokes, «My offspring have not tidied their rooms again.» Who does offspring mean here? | The neighbours | His parents | The dog | *His children
test: Scientists study how features pass from parents to their offspring. What does offspring mean? | Things that are always the same | The tools used in a lab | *The young that come from the parents | The parents themselves
test: A frog lays hundreds of eggs in a pond. Which word best describes the tadpoles that hatch from them? | *Offspring | Shade | Parents | Roots
exam: Is offspring singular or plural? | It has no meaning | Only plural | Only singular | *Both: the same form for one and for many
